{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1027658-any-suggestions-for-playing-a-high-grit-gangrel","id":1027658,"title":"Any suggestions for playing a high-Grit Gangrel?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-06T08:02:21-08:00","id":1027658,"title":"Any suggestions for playing a high-Grit Gangrel?","content":"So, the design goal for my latest vampire character is to play a Gangrel that will probably become sheriff who can take Air of Menace and/or Jack-Booted Thug and it feel appropriate. I normally play more cerebral and social characters, so it's going to be a challenge thematically and mechanically. Does anyone have any hints for pulling this archtype off well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:14:44-08:00","id":1027673,"title":"","content":"Sheriff needs to be social and/or intelligent too. I'd take physical as a secondary focus, tbh. Hounds are the thugs. That's advice one.<br /> <br /> I don't know how much time you have to prepare, but basically I'd advice you to watch as much (neo-)noir films as possible. Become a hard-boiled detective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:27:43-08:00","id":1027712,"title":"","content":"In terms of traits I was thinking mental secondary. Investigation 3, Occult 2, Science 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:40:05-08:00","id":1027718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1027658-any-suggestions-for-playing-a-high-grit-gangrel?p=1027673#post1027673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know how much time you have to prepare, but basically I'd advice you to watch as much (neo-)noir films as possible. Become a hard-boiled detective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give us any particular title to start with? I would appreciate it so much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:55:09-08:00","id":1027723,"title":"","content":"Gaslight. The Maltese Falcon. The Killers. Les Diaboliques or the 90s remake Diabolique. You also can't go wrong with Hitchcock movies like The 39 Steps, Vertigo, or Rear Window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T13:37:31-08:00","id":1027829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1027658-any-suggestions-for-playing-a-high-grit-gangrel?p=1027723#post1027723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaslight. The Maltese Falcon. The Killers. Les Diaboliques or the 90s remake Diabolique. You also can't go wrong with Hitchcock movies like The 39 Steps, Vertigo, or Rear Window.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not a bad era to draw a hard-nosed Ancilla from.<br /> <br /> Sheriff is a management/investigating position. You don't need to be a frothing Berserker to be &quot;hard&quot;, &quot;gritty&quot; or &quot;strong&quot;. In fact that would lead you to be fairly useless as a Sheriff. Besides detectives also check out underworld crime bosses of the same time period. Goons are needed for the type of work a Sheriff needs to do unless they are an Elder and thus able to do the job of several lesser kindred alone.<br /> <br /> Untouchables is another good movie title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-06-2017, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T15:58:06-08:00","id":1027888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1027658-any-suggestions-for-playing-a-high-grit-gangrel?p=1027829#post1027829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Untouchables is another good movie title.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They feed from one of our guys, we Ghoul one of theirs. That's the Chicago By Night way.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T07:19:12-08:00","id":1028138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1027658-any-suggestions-for-playing-a-high-grit-gangrel?p=1027718#post1027718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you give us any particular title to start with? I would appreciate it so much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Start of with Chinatown. Always. Then do the Big Lebowski. Make sure to also check out: The French Connection, Brick, and L.A. Confidential. The Nice Guys was quite fun too. There are scores of noir films, these are just some of my personal favourites that deal with detective work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T14:22:16-08:00","id":1028690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1027658-any-suggestions-for-playing-a-high-grit-gangrel#post1027658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the design goal for my latest vampire character is to play a Gangrel that will probably become sheriff who can take Air of Menace and/or Jack-Booted Thug and it feel appropriate. I normally play more cerebral and social characters, so it's going to be a challenge thematically and mechanically. Does anyone have any hints for pulling this archtype off well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cacophony Savvy. It's the perfect merit if you want a highly skilled Sheriff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:17:02-08:00","id":1028736,"title":"","content":"For the record, I drew the &quot;be the muscle&quot; straw. I probably wont be able to fit a ton of non-muscle stuff, but we also have a Mekhet and a reasonable exoectation of party cohesion.<br /> <br /> I plan to err on the side of keeping people in line and the political implications of being able to do that, and less murder mystery theature. I can fit maybe one non-physical aspect without tanking myself in other areas.<br /> <br /> That said, Cacaphony Savvy looks pretty great. Fitting politics in to my character will be a struggle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-08-2017, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:14:48-08:00","id":1029039,"title":"","content":"I don't see a problem with the sheriff being the muscle. I mean, ok, we're not going to talk about a super detective, but I think that role can be very different given the type of management the city has, the political landscape, the size, and other stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's how I see things. The Sheriff can be a skilled detective, BUT it some (I'd even say most) cases, the sheriff works for the Prince, they're law enforcement, the Prince's law. A sheriff's role could be an investigator's, but the Prince could also have spies to do that, and would have an easier time questioning other vampires who don't know they're investigating. Then, sure the sheriff is basically like a glorified hound, but there's nothing wrong with that. It also has advantages.<br /> <br /> The problem with the hard boiled type is that typically, they get no respect. People know they're smart, but they hate them for that, they just want them to stick their nose elsewhere, and I feel respect is an invaluable tool for the sheriff. Thing is, kicking ass is a god way to garner respect. The sheriff is authorized to use violence if it's for the prince. Even if they're not the best investigators, people will hesitate doing things if they know it can get them in trouble with a powerful gangrel. The probability of getting caught is less than with your typical mekhet spy, but dealing with the consequences can be a lot more troublesome. And anyway, not putting mental first doesn't mean your gangrel has to be an idiot. They can be a solid investigator. Breaking heads is also a method of investigation, especially when you're not tied down by things like warrants and stuff. A vampire the prince liked got killed. Everybody knows that nosferatu and his ghoul gang hated him, so the sheriff goes to kick down their door. What if they got framed ? With a little luck, they won't want any trouble and play really nice, hoping the sheriff decides not to break their knees, giving other leads worth investigating. With less luck, the sheriff beats them up and then starts asking questions for the same result. Is it a safe or good investigation method ? No, but it builds a reputation, and if it causes some other vampires to plot a revolution, then it's more story.<br /> <br /> One example I love that's not quite this but kinda is Max Payne 2. The game is one large investigation, and it's basically the hero going from place to place on pretty thin evidence, stumbling upon stuff he's not supposed to see and getting by simply by shooting everyone. In the end, he gets to the bottom of the investigation all the same. He missed all the subtle clues (which are in the game and paint a story the hero completely fails to see until the end, which is awesome), but he's enough of a tough guy that he gets the bad guy anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for respect, it depends how you play it. You could be the asshole who doesn't hesitate to walk over anyone who's in the bad place at the bad time to complete their mission. You'll be feared, but probably hated, but fear is already something. Or you could be the sheriff people KNOW could kick their ass easily, but doesn't do it unless it's absolutely necessary. Then, your strength will be feared, but also respected for being fair, kinda like a paladin (in a very different way), and the advantage of that is that even without that much social skill, people might figure it's safe to tell you stuff, and that's also a good investigation method.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, depends on how you're doing things, but getting minions might be good. The sheriff/hound I used in my first vampire game had three or four big ghouled dogs for example. First, it's always easier to be menacing when you have backup. Second, if you're going for a kind of thug, gang member enforcer aesthetic, it makes sense you'd have buddies helping you, as long as it's clear to everyone you're the boss. If they're human, it obviously bring the problem of the masquerade, but that's another matter. You could have an infant following you around, or another vampire you took under your wing. If you want to be respected, it can also show other vampires you take care of your own and you're not just a violent brute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 01-09-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}